1a launch dispatch: --ui=next, the default and --mini -> new window with their arguments; --ui=classic is refused
1b launch with last room only: opens Rooms, single primary "Return to Midnight library"
1c launch never autoplays (no command, no backend effect)
1c launch leaves no room active
1d Rooms lists every catalogue room
1e a catalogue room card enters that room (enter command, then Now)
1f launch while a room is active opens Now
1g launch into active room sends no mutating command
1h Return hero starts exactly the existing return, then Now
2a browsing, Mix, popovers, menu and collapsing Now send no playback command
2b browsing with no active room (Rooms/Listen/Now shortcut, popovers) sends nothing
2c browsing with no active room leaves it idle
3a Now (live radio) offers exactly the allowed controls
3b Next track is hidden (not merely disabled) on live radio
3c source chip present (Live radio)
3d room name shown in a serif face
3e Mix control carries a layer summary
3f now-playing line visible
3g Now is full-bleed art: nothing from Mix shown at rest
3h Now (library queue) offers the allowed controls including Next track
3i Next track is sensitive on a skippable library queue
3j source chip says Library
3k Next track sends one skip command (layer next)
4a Now text, tooltips and accessible names: no forbidden vocabulary
4b Timer popover: no forbidden vocabulary
4b Output popover: no forbidden vocabulary
4b Main menu popover: no forbidden vocabulary
4c Mix open: no forbidden vocabulary
4d Mix and Now use Music / Ambience / Scene
4e "Workspace 9" appears only as a Scene placement value
4f Mix row menu 'Music options': no forbidden vocabulary
4f Mix row menu 'Ambience options': no forbidden vocabulary
4f Mix row menu 'Change… Northern lake · offline Moonlit lake · offline Midnight Library · offline room Night Drive · offline room Northern Quiet · offline room Velvet Circuit · offline room After Hours · offline room Atomic Lounge · offline room Finnish Discoveries · offline room Wizarding Valley · offline room': no forbidden vocabulary
4f Mix row menu 'Scene options': no forbidden vocabulary
5a Pause sends the existing quiet (no minutes), nothing else
5b Pause quiets the layers (music Paused, not stopped)
5c the control becomes "Play the room"
5d Play sends the existing resume and playback resumes
5e the control returns to "Pause the room"
5f Main menu offers "Leave room"
5g Leave room sends the existing leave (fade-and-stop), not a bare stop
5h room is stopped after the leave fade and the window returns to browsing
6a Mix has rows Music, Ambience, Scene
6b each row names its source and a state
6c Music has level and mute
6d Ambience (outdoor sound) has level, mute and Window, and a plain Change… that opens Listen in ambience mode
6e Music row has no Window control
6f Scene has placement (Workspace 9 / Here), Moving picture, a close control and no level/mute
6j opening Mix and row menus sends no playback command
6g Music row menu: Stop always; Try again only after a failure; no Next track on live radio
6h Ambience row menu: Stop always; Try again only after a failure
6i Scene row menu: Stop always; Try again only after a failure
6k Music level slider sends a layer volume command that persists (35)
6l Music mute sends a layer command and the layer is muted
6m Ambience shows Window only for outdoor sounds (indoor sound hides it)
6n Scene can be closed (one layer command, picture stops, others play)
6o Mix offers "Save as my room…"
6p Save dialog opens with the room name prefilled
6q Save goes through the existing save command and stores the room
7a exactly one banner: one Try again and one Choose another
7b banner names the failing layer (Scene) and what keeps playing (Music)
7c banner vocabulary is clean
7d other layers keep playing
7e Try again re-runs only the failing layer (one picture/layer command; only start_picture runs)
7f Mix button carries a marker only while a layer failed (widget tree differs failed vs healthy)
7g banner clears once the layer starts
7h Choose another opens a chooser (popover, Mix or dialog) without changing playback
7i music failure banner names Music
8a the window sets room volume through the controller (room_volume command, value 50)
8b room volume scales Music and Ambience, keeping their ratio
8c per-layer levels persist unchanged under room volume
8d MPRIS Volume reads the room volume
8e listening-roomctl volume reads the same value (50)
8f listening-roomctl volume 70 sets it; the window slider follows
8g MPRIS Volume write sets the same value; window slider follows
8h saved rooms store room volume
8i entering the saved room restores its room volume
8j runbook documents the listening-roomctl volume verb
9a Timer popover offers Break 10 min, Wind down 30 min, Dim the scene 30 min, Cancel
9b no timer chip before a timer runs
9c Break 10 min sends the existing timed quiet with minutes 10
9d Break pauses the room and records a resume offer
9e a timer chip with time remaining appears in the header
9f Break confirms with a toast carrying Undo
9g Break never auto-resumes after its time (music still Paused); Play is offered
9h Wind down 30 min sends wind_down with minutes 30; chip shows it
9i Wind down toast carries Undo
9j Dim the scene 30 min sends one command with minutes 30 and shows a chip
9j2 Dim toast carries Undo
9k Cancel is available while a timer runs
9l Cancel stops the timers and removes the chip
9m Output popover lists the owned-stream outputs
9n Output popover has Test sound
9o Test sound plays a test sound and sends no playback command to the room
9p Output popover has a system volume control
9q system volume slider changes the system volume
10a loop plays muted while visible and pauses while the window is hidden
10b reduced motion: no playing video/media stream anywhere
10c reduced motion: no video widget or media paintable in the tree
10d reduced motion: still art is shown behind Now (non-flat pixels above the scrim; stdev 23.7 >= 8)
10e reduced motion: switching Rooms/Listen/Now runs no animated Gtk.Stack transition
11a Space pauses the room (quiet)
11b Space again resumes the room
11c Down lowers and Up raises room volume in Now
11d Esc closes Mix and stays in Now
11f Esc from Now returns to browsing
11g Ctrl+3 opens Now, Ctrl+2/Ctrl+1 leave it (accelerators registered)
11h Ctrl+1/Ctrl+2 reach browsing pages
11i each required control exists exactly once under its exact accessible name (Pause state)
11j "Play the room" appears when paused
11k every icon-only control has an explicit accessible name (Now, Mix, Rooms, Listen)
11l keyboard focus ring is visible over art (>=40 clearly changed pixels around the focused control)
12 layout at 1200x800: no control clipped or off-window, no horizontal scroll
12 layout at 800x700: no control clipped or off-window, no horizontal scroll
